  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Commercial folk movement of mid-1960s Santiago in which vocal groups such as Los Cuatro Cuartos, Las Cuatro Brujas and Los de Ramón sang cuecas, tonadas and new songs in folk rhythms in polished close-harmony arrangements for radio, television and LP. It ran alongside, and was soon overtaken by, the nueva canción chilena.",
